      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes requested** — See inline comments for details. [[trajectory](go/traj/a3ec6697-a1b5-4400-a51c-796f47540132)]\n\n### Review Summary\n\n*   **Functionality:** The migration to `DT_INST_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY` is mostly correct. However, it introduces a dangerous silent failure mode where the `CROS_SYSTEM` device is completely dropped from the build if the devicetree node is missing. This explains the binary size changes for `pujjolo`, `deku`, and others mentioned in the commit message. See inline comment for a `BUILD_ASSERT` suggestion to catch this at compile-time.\n*   **Security:** No security issues identified.\n*   **Style:** The style conforms to Zephyr driver standards.\n*   **Testing:** Native sim and emulator devicetrees were correctly updated to include the new node. \n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL is appropriately sized and scoped to focus solely on the devicetree instantiation migration.\n\n### Action Items\n1. Add `BUILD_ASSERT(DT_NUM_INST_STATUS_OKAY(DT_DRV_COMPAT) \u003d\u003d 1, ...)` to all updated driver files to prevent silent omission.\n2. Fix the missing `cros-ec,cros-system` nodes in the devicetrees for the boards that showed binary differences (`pujjolo`, `deku`, etc.).",
