      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Since `cros_system` is an essential driver for the EC, silently skipping its instantiation if the devicetree node is missing will lead to runtime crashes when `device_get_binding(\"CROS_SYSTEM\")` returns `NULL`. \n\nThe build differences mentioned in the commit message (`pujjolo`, `deku`, etc.) are almost certainly because these boards are missing the `cros-ec,cros-system` node in their devicetree (e.g., they might be using an `intel_ish` build which didn\u0027t get the node, or they don\u0027t include `npcx_cros.dtsi`). When the node is missing, `DT_INST_FOREACH_STATUS_OKAY` evaluates to nothing, and the device is silently dropped from the binary.\n\nI highly recommend adding a `BUILD_ASSERT` here and in all other SoC drivers to ensure the node is always present and only defined once. This will cause a compile-time failure for any board missing the node, rather than a silent runtime failure:\n\n```c\nBUILD_ASSERT(DT_NUM_INST_STATUS_OKAY(DT_DRV_COMPAT) \u003d\u003d 1,\n\t     \"Exactly one cros-ec,cros-system node is required\");\n```",
